<h2>Who runs the app</h2>
<p>LevelCast is developed and run by {{ site.author }}, Israel. Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

<h2>What the app does</h2>
<p>LevelCast plays podcasts from public feeds and processes the audio on your device to even out the volume between speakers. It does not host content and does not distribute it.</p>

<h2>The content isn't ours</h2>
<p>Every episode belongs to its producer and comes from their server. The rights, accuracy and responsibility for the content are the producer's. We don't edit, filter or choose what gets published.</p>

<h2>What's free</h2>
<p>Search, following, listening with strong levelling, a queue of up to three episodes, intro skip and moment capture are free and will stay free.</p>
<p>For the first two weeks from the app's first launch on the device, everything is open, including Pro AI, with no payment and no sign-up. The count starts at the first launch, and deleting and reinstalling the app does not start it again. When the two weeks end nothing is charged: you keep what is free, or what you bought.</p>

<h2>The paid plans</h2>
<p>LevelCast Pro adds a levelling setting per show, an unlimited queue, advance downloads, speeds above <span dir="ltr">1.5×</span>, pace matching, the sleep timer, alerts for new episodes and background refresh. iOS decides when background refresh runs, so there is no commitment to how often it happens.</p>
<p>LevelCast Pro AI includes all of Pro, and adds live transcript, search inside an episode and key points (selected sentences from the transcript). Transcription runs on the phone only, so it is available only on a device that can recognise speech locally in the episode's language. It is worth trying during the two open weeks before buying.</p>
<p>Each plan is offered with monthly or yearly billing. The price is shown on the purchase screen before payment, and it is the final price, including VAT.</p>

<h2>A free month on the yearly plan</h2>
<p>The yearly plan comes with a first month free, once per person under Apple's rules. Unless you cancel at least 24 hours before that month ends, the full yearly price is charged and a year of subscription begins. The monthly plan has no free month. If you buy a different subscription during the free month, what remains of it is forfeited. The two open weeks at the start are not part of this offer and are not forfeited by a purchase.</p>

<h2>Renewal and cancellation</h2>
<p>Billing goes through your Apple ID account and renews automatically at the end of each period, unless you cancel at least 24 hours before it ends. You can cancel in your Apple ID settings, or from the subscription screen inside the app, which opens the same Apple screen. After cancelling, access continues until the end of the period you paid for, and there is no further charge.</p>

<h2>Refunds</h2>
<p>Payment is collected by Apple, so refund requests go to Apple at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. This does not limit any right you have under Israel's Consumer Protection Law. If you run into a problem, write to us and we'll help.</p>

<h2>Fair use</h2>
<p>You may not use the app to redistribute producers' content, or to bypass restrictions a producer has placed on their feed.</p>

<h2>No warranty</h2>
<p>The app is provided as is. There is no commitment that a particular episode will be found, that a particular feed will be available, or that the processing will suit every recording.</p>

<h2>License agreement</h2>
<p>Use of the app is also subject to <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Apple's standard licensed application end user license agreement</a>.</p>

<h2>Governing law</h2>
<p>The laws of the State of Israel.</p>
